                    {
                        "sense_id": "27e85ee5-639d-332d-97fe-82e6ed7f7346",
                        "entry_id": "a6d5a740-ff32-30c5-8dc8-922f4af4fc08",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Roughly spherical in shape; globe-shaped."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "16a7bf12-117d-4953-b2c2-be6a2e16037b",
                                "sense_id": "27e85ee5-639d-332d-97fe-82e6ed7f7346",
                                "text": "\"Nary a spot,\" interrupted E. R. Coglan, flippantly. \"The terrestrial, globular, planetary hunk of matter, slightly flattened at the poles, and known as the Earth, is my abode.[…]\""
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "6440235a-9984-48e9-9a4d-d9dee2343acf",
                                "sense_id": "27e85ee5-639d-332d-97fe-82e6ed7f7346",
                                "text": "Podson's globular stare assured any woman that the bargain was sacred. It was solemn, intent, opaque; it was also slightly mesmeric, which is to say that it gave out everything and took in nothing."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "6997024f-84e2-4562-8756-09038aca7663",
                                "sense_id": "27e85ee5-639d-332d-97fe-82e6ed7f7346",
                                "text": "Globular lights, painted a dark green, hang from under the fancy iron eaves, unlit for centuries . . ."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
